{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CghARQoh7gGtJ3oKoEa6X", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "For identity resolution, AuditService relies on **UserService**, which reads from **UsersPostgresDatabase**. One thing to know up front: the graph records the dependency itself, but none of its relationships are labelled \"identity resolution.\" I'm treating UserService as the identity provider because it's AuditService's only user-related dependency.\n\n**The chain:**\n\n1. **AuditService \u2192 UserService** (DEPENDS_ON). This is AuditService's only dependency on another service.\n2. **UserService \u2192 UsersPostgresDatabase** (STORES). User data lives in this database.\n3. **ORDER_DB_URL** sets the connection to UserService's read replica. The name is misleading: it says \"ORDER\" but it configures UserService. It was never renamed because three deployment scripts still read it. Be careful before renaming or changing it.\n\n**Not part of identity resolution:**\n- **AuditIcebergTable** is where AuditService stores its audit records (STORES). It's AuditService's own storage, not part of user lookup.\n- No configuration keys are recorded directly on AuditService.\n\nIf UserService, UsersPostgresDatabase or ORDER_DB_URL goes down or is misconfigured, AuditService loses identity resolution."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 368, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4842, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 368}, "output_tokens": 402, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "210d3cd3-b57f-4d2e-a09f-9fbc55e061b0", "uuid": "0063b390-cca9-4097-a0e9-09a2bca1234d", "timestamp": "2026-11-04T03:17:1