{"type": "result", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "num_turns": 5, "result": "For identity resolution, AuditService relies on **UserService**, which reads from **UsersPostgresDatabase**. One thing to know up front: the graph records the dependency itself, but none of its relationships are labelled \"identity resolution.\" I'm treating UserService as the identity provider because it's AuditService's only user-related dependency.\n\n**The chain:**\n\n1. **AuditService \u2192 UserService** (DEPENDS_ON). This is AuditService's only dependency on another service.\n2. **UserService \u2192 UsersPostgresDatabase** (STORES). User data lives in this database.\n3. **ORDER_DB_URL** sets the connection to UserService's read replica. The name is misleading: it says \"ORDER\" but it configures UserService. It was never renamed because three deployment scripts still read it. Be careful before renaming or changing it.\n\n**Not part of identity resolution:**\n- **AuditIcebergTable** is where AuditService stores its audit records (STORES). It's AuditService's own storage, not part of user lookup.\n- No configuration keys are recorded directly on AuditService.\n\nIf UserService, UsersPostgresDatabase or ORDER_DB_URL goes down or is misconfigured, AuditService loses identity resolution.", "usage": {"input_tokens": 6, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3552, "cache_read_input_tokens": 10980, "output_tokens": 745, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 54}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3552, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "global", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 402, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4842, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 368, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 368}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard", "fallback_credit": null}, "duration_ms": 13639}
